=== Agent Answer ===
Argumentative zoning (AZ), also called rhetorical sentence classification, is a process of assigning rhetorical status to extracted sentences [1]. In this paper, AZ is described as an important task in scientific paper analysis [7], and an example annotation scheme assigns seven categories of rhetorical status to full sentences: aim, contrast, own, background, other, basis and textual [3].
